$DIR/main.p:16:10: the field rows.data[i] of a synced[DB] is read here through a view that is not valid here: mu, which guards it, was not held from the load of the view to here
    The field rows.data[i] of a synced[DB] is read at main.p:16 in reader
    through a view loaded from shared memory. A view loaded from memory a lock
    guards stays valid only while a lock held at the load stays held: an Unlock,
    an RUnlock or a Wait of it, or a call that may release it, ends the view,
    even if the lock is taken again. Once the lock is released another task may
    change, move or free what the view points to.
    Go leaves data races to a run-time detector that a program must be run
    under, and a racing Go program can see values half written. Plutonium tasks
    run in parallel with no such detector, so safe code must be free of data
    races, and the compiler checks it from the program itself, with no
    annotations.
    Keep the lock held from the load of the view to its last use, or load the
    view again after taking the lock
    (see "Data race freedom" in the Plutonium spec, section 19.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3501" for a longer explanation)
